<h2>Segment 216 &mdash; the self as seed basis</h2>
<div class="pair">
<div class="tib"><div class="lab">TIBETAN (WYLIE)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s216S">ji ltar <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w1"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s216m1">kun gzhi</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s216m2">rnam shes</span></span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w2">khas len pa</span> rnams kyi ltar na, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w3"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s216m3">nyon</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s216m4">yid</span></span> kyis <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w4">nga</span>&#x27;o snyam du <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w5">dmigs pa</span>&#x27;i gzhir gyur pa&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w6"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s216m5">kun gzhi</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s216m6">rnam shes</span></span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w7">bag chags</span> kyi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w8">gnas</span> su <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w9">&#x27;dod pa</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w10">de bzhin du</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w11">lugs</span> &#x27;dis <span class="u additive" data-d="6" data-l="s216p1">kyang</span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s216c1">nga&#x27;o snyam pa tsam gyi blo lhan skyes</span> kyi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w12">dmigs pa</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w13"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s216m7">de</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s216m8">nyid</span></span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w14">bag chags</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w15">sgo ba</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w16">gzhir</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w17">bzhed</span> do</span>
</div>
<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s216S">According to those who <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w2">accept</span> the idea of a <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w1"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s216m1">foundation</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s216m2">consciousness</span></span>, the thing called &quot;<span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w3"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s216m3">afflicted</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s216m4">mind</span></span>&quot; <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w5">focuses on</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w6"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s216m5">foundation</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s216m6">consciousness</span></span> and holds it to be &quot;<span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w4">me</span>&quot;; they <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w9">say</span> that this foundation consciousness then is the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w8">place</span> where the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w7">mental seeds</span> stay. In our [Madhyamika] <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w11">school</span> <span class="u additive" data-d="6" data-l="s216p1">too</span> we have a <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w10">similar</span> concept; we <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w17">say</span> that the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w16">base</span> which is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w15">stained</span> with the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w14">mental seed</span> is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w13"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s216m8">exactly</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s216m7">that</span> thing</span> that you <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s216w12">focus on</span> with your <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s216c1">simple, natural awareness of yourself</span> and call &quot;me.&quot;</span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; <p>PROVISIONAL Codex English-first proposal. The opening Tibetan relation <code>ji ltar ... kyi ltar na</code> is distributed around the people compared; rather than assign the single English <i>According to</i> to one half or absorb supplied <i>those who</i> and <i>the idea of</i> into a broad phrase, both relation markers and the plural/nominal frame are omitted. The first two Tibetan foundation-consciousness compounds select the first two of three English occurrences. GMR repeats the second as <i>this foundation consciousness</i>; the once-at-cursor rule leaves that explanatory repetition unwrapped.</p><p><code>nyon yid</code> supplies only <i>afflicted mind</i>; <i>the thing called</i> is added framing. <code>dmigs pa</code> owns the lexical phrasal verbs <i>focuses on</i>/<i>focus on</i>, while the agentive and English participants remain outside. Within <code>nga'o snyam du</code>, only <code>nga</code> is separately secure as the first <i>me</i>; <i>holds it to be</i> distributes the thought construction and is omitted rather than assigned to <code>snyam</code> or falsely nulled. The single <code>gnas</code> is banked once as <i>place</i>, leaving the repeated verbal <i>stay</i> unwrapped.</p><p>The second self-awareness expression is retained whole at phrase depth as <i>simple, natural awareness of yourself</i>; supplied possessive <i>your</i> and the later explanatory <i>and call "me"</i> remain unwrapped. <code>'dis</code> and its shifted participant <i>our</i>/<i>we</i> are omitted; <code>bzhed</code> owns only <i>say</i>. The base/stain/seed relation is split into exact content words without wrapping <i>the</i>, <i>which is</i>, or <i>with</i>. Exact C16 repetition and the differently translated ILL parallel establish no source correction; no erratum is proposed.</p></div>
